1
00:00:42,355 --> 00:00:46,067
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:00:51,406 --> 00:00:52,824
‎It's my fault.

3
00:00:55,410 --> 00:00:56,619
‎Because of me…

4
00:01:35,909 --> 00:01:37,702
‎EPISODE 5

5
00:01:40,413 --> 00:01:41,789
‎Mr. Ma?

6
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:47,003
‎Gang-uk.

7
00:01:49,464 --> 00:01:50,423
‎Oh, no…

8
00:01:53,301 --> 00:01:54,552
‎Because of me,

9
00:01:56,262 --> 00:01:58,806
‎you turned into a ghost already
‎and came to see me?

10
00:02:01,768 --> 00:02:02,769
‎Oh, no…

11
00:02:06,105 --> 00:02:07,565
‎Oh, gosh…

12
00:02:57,115 --> 00:02:59,325
‎I'm not a ghost.

13
00:03:01,369 --> 00:03:02,495
‎I'm alive.

14
00:03:14,048 --> 00:03:16,009
‎But before, I definitely saw you…

15
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:23,766
‎Gang-uk!

16
00:03:25,601 --> 00:03:27,395
‎-Charge to 200 joules.
‎-Charging to 200.

17
00:03:28,396 --> 00:03:29,939
‎-Clear.
‎-Mr. Ma!

18
00:03:31,024 --> 00:03:32,316
‎-Mr. Ma!
‎-Clear.

19
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:33,818
‎Mr. Ma.

20
00:03:33,901 --> 00:03:34,777
‎Clear.

21
00:03:40,283 --> 00:03:42,327
‎It worked. We have a pulse.

22
00:03:43,953 --> 00:03:45,538
‎He's back. He's okay.

23
00:03:52,837 --> 00:03:54,672
‎You're alive?

24
00:04:05,099 --> 00:04:08,353
‎Are you sure you're really alive?

25
00:04:08,436 --> 00:04:09,896
‎I am.

26
00:04:11,814 --> 00:04:13,358
‎My head hurts a bit,

27
00:04:14,525 --> 00:04:17,278
‎but I'm quite all right
‎for someone who got hit by a car.

28
00:04:22,450 --> 00:04:26,162
‎I thought you'd actually died
‎because of me.

29
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:28,915
‎Do you know how scared I was?

30
00:04:31,125 --> 00:04:31,959
‎I'm sorry.

31
00:04:32,043 --> 00:04:33,795
‎You're not hurt anywhere, right?

32
00:04:38,007 --> 00:04:39,008
‎Mr. Ma!

33
00:04:42,470 --> 00:04:43,429
‎You need to come.

34
00:04:48,142 --> 00:04:50,478
‎-Is there something wrong?
‎-No.

35
00:04:50,561 --> 00:04:54,232
‎There's nothing
‎terribly wrong with him right now,

36
00:04:54,315 --> 00:04:57,485
‎but the doctor wants to run
‎a few tests, just in case.

37
00:04:58,528 --> 00:04:59,987
‎That gave us all quite a scare.

38
00:05:00,696 --> 00:05:02,115
‎You still seem to be in shock.

39
00:05:05,284 --> 00:05:07,703
‎We should get going then.

40
00:05:07,787 --> 00:05:09,247
‎Take good care of Mr. Ma for us.

41
00:05:09,330 --> 00:05:10,331
‎You go on ahead.

42
00:05:10,415 --> 00:05:12,583
‎-I don't mind staying behind.
‎-What?

43
00:05:12,667 --> 00:05:14,085
‎It's been a long day. Go on home.

44
00:05:15,128 --> 00:05:17,547
‎It's late, and your wife will be worried.

45
00:05:17,630 --> 00:05:19,465
‎Why would she worry
‎with everything that's happening?

46
00:05:19,549 --> 00:05:20,967
‎One of us should stay behind.

47
00:05:21,050 --> 00:05:22,218
‎Yes, that one person…

48
00:05:24,303 --> 00:05:25,847
‎What? Oh, she's…

49
00:05:25,930 --> 00:05:27,723
‎-She's going to stay?
‎-Yes.

50
00:05:27,807 --> 00:05:29,434
‎-Yes, she's staying.
‎-She is?

51
00:05:29,517 --> 00:05:31,853
‎Take good care of him for us. Thank you.

52
00:05:31,936 --> 00:05:34,272
‎-At least until he falls asleep…
‎-Take care.

53
00:05:34,856 --> 00:05:35,690
‎Hey.

54
00:05:39,110 --> 00:05:42,363
‎Drink lots of water to flush
‎the contrast medium out of your system.

55
00:05:42,446 --> 00:05:43,948
‎You'll be hospitalized for the night,

56
00:05:44,031 --> 00:05:47,535
‎and the doctor will give you the results
‎in the morning.

57
00:05:47,618 --> 00:05:48,786
‎Okay. Thank you.

58
00:05:48,870 --> 00:05:49,954
‎You're welcome.

59
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:55,960
‎CT IMAGING ROOM

60
00:06:16,814 --> 00:06:18,065
‎You're still here, Yeo-ri?

61
00:06:18,941 --> 00:06:20,359
‎The one month isn't up yet.

62
00:06:20,943 --> 00:06:24,280
‎It's not over until the moon
‎disappears at dawn.

63
00:06:26,866 --> 00:06:28,075
‎Try to keep up.

64
00:06:28,576 --> 00:06:29,619
‎Okay.

65
00:07:08,699 --> 00:07:10,701
‎They agreed not to come into your room.

66
00:07:11,285 --> 00:07:13,120
‎How did you make them agree to that?

67
00:07:14,038 --> 00:07:15,081
‎I told them the usual,

68
00:07:15,164 --> 00:07:17,625
‎that they can come to my place
‎if they really want to talk.

69
00:07:19,752 --> 00:07:22,338
‎Did this happen
‎because we celebrated a day early?

70
00:07:23,673 --> 00:07:27,051
‎What's meant to happen happens,
‎regardless of such things.

71
00:07:27,134 --> 00:07:30,304
‎Only seeing and hearing
‎what everyone else does…

72
00:07:31,556 --> 00:07:33,724
‎I can't believe
‎that's something worth celebrating.

73
00:07:36,561 --> 00:07:37,562
‎Yeo-ri.

74
00:07:38,062 --> 00:07:40,648
‎The moon will set soon.
‎You must be exhausted, so go home.

75
00:07:42,275 --> 00:07:45,278
‎I'd rather stay where I can be at ease
‎than go home and be anxious.

76
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:50,241
‎Your month is almost up for good,
‎so I'll rest here with you.

77
00:07:58,249 --> 00:08:01,419
‎I didn't get to ask you
‎because things got a bit hectic.

78
00:08:01,502 --> 00:08:03,129
‎Why did Park Seung-jae abduct you?

79
00:08:03,212 --> 00:08:04,714
‎I'm the one who put him behind bars.

80
00:08:06,507 --> 00:08:09,385
‎I think he caught on to my secret.

81
00:08:10,553 --> 00:08:11,762
‎But how?

82
00:08:13,431 --> 00:08:14,599
‎That's a family matter.

83
00:08:17,602 --> 00:08:21,147
‎How did you know where to find me anyway?

84
00:08:22,773 --> 00:08:23,608
‎Well…

85
00:08:27,361 --> 00:08:29,989
‎FIND ME

86
00:08:30,072 --> 00:08:32,950
‎FIND ME

87
00:08:34,452 --> 00:08:36,412
‎I think a ghost told me.

88
00:08:37,455 --> 00:08:39,123
‎-A ghost?
‎-Yes.

89
00:08:40,833 --> 00:08:41,667
‎Come in.

90
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,045
‎Hello.

91
00:08:44,128 --> 00:08:46,589
‎-I'm here to change your IV bag.
‎-Okay.

92
00:08:47,632 --> 00:08:49,967
‎Can you be gentle this time?
‎It hurt earlier.

93
00:08:50,051 --> 00:08:51,969
‎-I'm scared of needles.
‎-Okay.

94
00:08:52,053 --> 00:08:56,974
‎HANKUK NATIONAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

95
00:09:32,551 --> 00:09:33,886
‎Because of me,

96
00:09:34,470 --> 00:09:36,889
‎you turned into a ghost already
‎and came to see me?

97
00:09:41,102 --> 00:09:42,436
‎Oh, no…

98
00:10:47,209 --> 00:10:49,295
‎I think the one month is up now.

99
00:10:51,005 --> 00:10:53,424
‎I should go do some stretching.

100
00:11:10,816 --> 00:11:13,569
‎REGIONAL EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

101
00:11:13,652 --> 00:11:16,197
‎I told you I'd be fine.
‎You didn't have to worry.

102
00:11:17,364 --> 00:11:20,659
‎Still, I feel much better
‎after seeing the results myself.

103
00:11:24,872 --> 00:11:27,833
‎I guess today is day one
‎of not seeing ghosts.

104
00:11:28,542 --> 00:11:30,252
‎Yes, based on my experiences so far.

105
00:11:30,336 --> 00:11:31,462
‎I really won't see them

106
00:11:32,338 --> 00:11:33,422
‎anymore, right?

107
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:40,554
‎I find it really hard to believe,

108
00:11:40,638 --> 00:11:44,767
‎but knowing such supernatural beings
‎exist in our world today…

109
00:11:45,935 --> 00:11:47,061
‎I know, right?

110
00:11:48,354 --> 00:11:51,023
‎Anyway, congratulations.

111
00:11:51,649 --> 00:11:53,734
‎You can go back to your normal life now.

112
00:11:53,817 --> 00:11:57,029
‎I feel bad that I'm the only one
‎who gets off like this.

113
00:11:57,112 --> 00:11:57,947
‎Don't be.

114
00:11:58,531 --> 00:12:02,576
‎It's a relief that you, at least,
‎can escape this fate.

115
00:12:04,745 --> 00:12:05,913
‎Yeo-ri.

116
00:12:08,707 --> 00:12:11,043
‎Even if you were to
‎continue seeing ghosts,

117
00:12:11,126 --> 00:12:13,128
‎that wouldn't mean I'd stop seeing them.

118
00:12:16,048 --> 00:12:17,800
‎We can't shake hands anymore,

119
00:12:19,009 --> 00:12:20,261
‎so let's part ways here.

120
00:12:21,971 --> 00:12:25,391
‎From now on,
‎let's never cross paths again.

121
00:12:40,573 --> 00:12:41,865
‎Take care.

122
00:12:43,951 --> 00:12:44,910
‎Thanks for everything.

123
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:05,449
‎REHEAT THE RICE AND SOUP AND EAT WELL

124
00:14:15,167 --> 00:14:18,045
‎From now on,
‎let's never cross paths again.

125
00:14:19,254 --> 00:14:20,339
‎Take care.

126
00:14:22,007 --> 00:14:23,092
‎Thanks for everything.

127
00:14:30,015 --> 00:14:32,810
‎Just to be clear,
‎I never told you to kidnap her.

128
00:14:33,644 --> 00:14:36,146
‎And don't call me like this again,
‎not even through your lawyer.

129
00:14:36,230 --> 00:14:37,523
‎Wait, Ha-ri, I--

130
00:14:38,273 --> 00:14:39,608
‎Hello? Cheon Ha-ri!

131
00:14:40,275 --> 00:14:41,110
‎Damn it.

132
00:14:50,869 --> 00:14:52,997
‎The assemblyman said
‎he can't help you anymore.

133
00:14:53,580 --> 00:14:55,958
‎He told me to inform you
‎that there'd be no more favors.

134
00:14:58,961 --> 00:14:59,878
‎Wait…

135
00:15:00,754 --> 00:15:02,423
‎Damn it.

136
00:15:07,136 --> 00:15:09,263
‎Mr. Ma. Are you all right?

137
00:15:09,346 --> 00:15:11,515
‎I'm still a bit sore. Did you have lunch?

138
00:15:11,598 --> 00:15:14,059
‎I told you I put in a day off for you.

139
00:15:14,143 --> 00:15:16,145
‎Why are you so stubborn?

140
00:15:16,228 --> 00:15:18,897
‎Come on, there's a warrant hearing later.

141
00:15:18,981 --> 00:15:22,818
‎I told you the chief prosecutor
‎can handle that for you.

142
00:15:23,527 --> 00:15:25,529
‎-Mr. Ma.
‎-Yeah?

143
00:15:26,196 --> 00:15:27,781
‎You need to see this.

144
00:15:27,865 --> 00:15:28,741
‎Why?

145
00:15:29,616 --> 00:15:30,784
‎What is it?

146
00:15:30,868 --> 00:15:32,286
‎PARK SEUNG-JAE ABDUCTED CEO CHEON YEO-RI,
‎MOTIVE UNDER INVESTIGATION

147
00:15:32,369 --> 00:15:34,663
‎Reporters are already
‎swarming outside Reina.

148
00:15:34,747 --> 00:15:36,040
‎PARK SEUNG-JAE ABDUCTED CEO CHEON YEO-RI

149
00:15:36,123 --> 00:15:37,708
‎Please leave.
‎We'll explain some other time.

150
00:15:43,881 --> 00:15:44,715
‎Mr. Ma.

151
00:15:44,798 --> 00:15:46,633
‎-She won't do any interviews.
‎-Just let us…

152
00:15:46,717 --> 00:15:49,178
‎-No, you can't…
‎-Will you stop it?

153
00:15:49,261 --> 00:15:52,014
‎-Just a few shots.
‎-No way!

154
00:15:52,097 --> 00:15:54,725
‎-Stop! Get back!
‎-Don't take any photos!

155
00:15:54,808 --> 00:15:56,727
‎-You can't.
‎-No photos or filming!

156
00:15:56,810 --> 00:15:58,979
‎-Can we get a comment?
‎-No photos, please!

157
00:15:59,063 --> 00:16:00,731
‎-What happened?
‎-Don't take photos!

158
00:16:00,814 --> 00:16:03,275
‎-Is everything we heard true?
‎-I said, no photos.

159
00:16:03,358 --> 00:16:05,611
‎-Any further comments?
‎-Just a brief statement, please.

160
00:16:05,694 --> 00:16:07,654
‎Gosh, there are so many of them.

161
00:16:07,738 --> 00:16:09,239
‎-How are you now?
‎-We won't take long.

162
00:16:09,323 --> 00:16:11,366
‎-Any comments, please?
‎-Please stop.

163
00:16:19,208 --> 00:16:21,376
‎-Can you tell us anything?
‎-Please step back.

164
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:24,171
‎-Please step back.
‎-Excuse me, Ms. Cheon.

165
00:16:24,254 --> 00:16:25,881
‎-Move back.
‎-Can you do an interview?

166
00:16:43,357 --> 00:16:44,608
‎Are you dating Ms. Cheon?

167
00:16:44,691 --> 00:16:46,693
‎Should there be
‎any unverified information,

168
00:16:48,695 --> 00:16:50,697
‎speculative articles,
‎or photos distributed…

169
00:16:52,950 --> 00:16:55,536
‎Reina will take strong legal action.

170
00:16:56,203 --> 00:16:58,413
‎Direct your questions
‎to the secretaries' office,

171
00:17:00,499 --> 00:17:01,834
‎and please step back.

172
00:17:29,403 --> 00:17:30,696
‎I should've gotten here sooner.

173
00:17:39,997 --> 00:17:41,081
‎Are you all right?

174
00:17:41,623 --> 00:17:42,457
‎Yeah.

175
00:17:43,667 --> 00:17:44,710
‎Thanks.

176
00:17:56,638 --> 00:17:59,266
‎I'm sorry for causing you concern.

177
00:18:00,475 --> 00:18:01,643
‎Were you hurt anywhere?

178
00:18:02,811 --> 00:18:04,479
‎Should I call Dr. Kim?

179
00:18:05,397 --> 00:18:07,566
‎Let's get you admitted for some tests.

180
00:18:07,649 --> 00:18:08,525
‎No.

181
00:18:08,609 --> 00:18:11,653
‎There's an inspection for the GA21 banquet
‎by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs today.

182
00:18:12,404 --> 00:18:14,239
‎I came to work thinking only of that.

183
00:18:15,490 --> 00:18:16,992
‎We'll take strong action

184
00:18:17,659 --> 00:18:21,538
‎against not only Park Seung-jae,
‎but his father Assemblyman Park too.

185
00:18:22,456 --> 00:18:24,666
‎Don't worry about them
‎and look after yourself.

186
00:18:25,375 --> 00:18:26,210
‎Okay.

187
00:18:26,293 --> 00:18:30,047
‎I do have more questions to ask you,

188
00:18:30,130 --> 00:18:31,548
‎but let's leave it at that for today.

189
00:18:32,132 --> 00:18:34,509
‎Just handle the inspection,
‎then go home and rest.

190
00:18:36,178 --> 00:18:37,554
‎Don't worry about me, Grandma.

191
00:18:45,771 --> 00:18:46,855
‎What is it?

192
00:18:47,648 --> 00:18:49,066
‎What do you want?

193
00:18:49,149 --> 00:18:50,025
‎What?

194
00:18:50,609 --> 00:18:52,319
‎The secretaries confirmed it.

195
00:18:53,070 --> 00:18:57,324
‎You visited Park Seung-jae in prison twice
‎before he kidnapped me.

196
00:18:57,824 --> 00:18:59,868
‎Is that when you put him up to kidnap me?

197
00:18:59,952 --> 00:19:01,411
‎What do you mean, kidnap you?

198
00:19:01,495 --> 00:19:02,454
‎Even if I…

199
00:19:04,915 --> 00:19:06,708
‎Yes, I did visit him.

200
00:19:07,209 --> 00:19:09,169
‎But only because he begged me to.

201
00:19:09,253 --> 00:19:11,255
‎I only went and saw him.

202
00:19:11,964 --> 00:19:14,549
‎Park Seung-jae isn't
‎the tight-lipped type,

203
00:19:15,259 --> 00:19:17,219
‎so I'm sure the investigation
‎will reveal everything.

204
00:19:18,679 --> 00:19:19,763
‎Cheon Ha-ri.

205
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:25,727
‎You can tell a lot about a person
‎by what they do.

206
00:19:26,895 --> 00:19:31,733
‎Take a long, hard look
‎at everything you've done so far,

207
00:19:31,817 --> 00:19:32,859
‎because that's your future.

208
00:19:33,610 --> 00:19:36,321
‎What do you mean?
‎You're not making any sense.

209
00:19:36,405 --> 00:19:38,198
‎If you don't understand,
‎just memorize it.

210
00:19:38,282 --> 00:19:40,117
‎"Don't do bad things."

211
00:19:41,159 --> 00:19:41,994
‎Also,

212
00:19:42,577 --> 00:19:44,538
‎I'm not letting this slide.

213
00:19:45,455 --> 00:19:46,623
‎Don't think I did.

214
00:20:00,679 --> 00:20:01,722
‎Was Ha-ri behind it?

215
00:20:02,681 --> 00:20:05,767
‎She did visit him in prison,
‎but that doesn't prove anything.

216
00:20:07,561 --> 00:20:09,771
‎By the way, what are you doing in Seoul?

217
00:20:09,855 --> 00:20:11,648
‎That took you long enough.

218
00:20:12,524 --> 00:20:14,026
‎I called you as soon as I arrived.

219
00:20:15,110 --> 00:20:17,738
‎G1A Group is trying to sell Fiel Seoul.

220
00:20:18,488 --> 00:20:20,407
‎-Is CL going to acquire it?
‎-Yeah.

221
00:20:20,490 --> 00:20:23,994
‎It's the only big resort brand
‎in the northern Seoul area.

222
00:20:24,578 --> 00:20:27,706
‎I heard their debt ratio
‎is on the higher side.

223
00:20:27,789 --> 00:20:29,166
‎That's true,

224
00:20:29,249 --> 00:20:32,419
‎but we have a financial arm
‎that can handle the aftermath.

225
00:20:33,420 --> 00:20:36,340
‎Anyway, do you know how shocked I was
‎during my breakfast meeting?

226
00:20:37,883 --> 00:20:40,177
‎First, it was in Jeju Island,
‎and now this.

227
00:20:40,260 --> 00:20:41,970
‎Things keep going wrong.

228
00:20:42,054 --> 00:20:43,555
‎What happened in Jeju was on us.

229
00:20:45,057 --> 00:20:48,852
‎I think I'll be in Seoul
‎until the acquisition is finalized.

230
00:20:48,935 --> 00:20:50,228
‎You'll call me, right?

231
00:20:50,812 --> 00:20:51,730
‎What?

232
00:20:52,314 --> 00:20:53,565
‎I knew it.

233
00:20:53,648 --> 00:20:55,150
‎You owe me a meal.

234
00:20:56,234 --> 00:20:57,069
‎Right.

235
00:20:57,152 --> 00:20:58,528
‎Yes, of course.

236
00:20:59,363 --> 00:21:00,947
‎Well, when are you free?

237
00:21:03,283 --> 00:21:07,162
‎Instead of going somewhere to eat,
‎you can accompany me elsewhere.

238
00:21:07,871 --> 00:21:09,081
‎Yeeon Museum of Art.

239
00:21:10,082 --> 00:21:12,459
‎They're unveiling an artifact
‎they excavated recently.

240
00:21:12,542 --> 00:21:14,711
‎I have a meeting there
‎that my mother arranged.

241
00:21:15,712 --> 00:21:16,546
‎Yeeon?

242
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:19,383
‎The director there is pretty influential.

243
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:22,803
‎This new artifact should interest you too,

244
00:21:22,886 --> 00:21:24,846
‎since it's not entirely unrelated
‎to your major.

245
00:21:25,764 --> 00:21:26,848
‎What is it?

246
00:21:26,932 --> 00:21:28,975
‎I'll send you a link
‎to the director's interview.

247
00:21:34,648 --> 00:21:36,441
‎From what my mom told me,

248
00:21:36,525 --> 00:21:39,694
‎she seems to be seeing
‎some prosecutor pretty often.

249
00:21:46,326 --> 00:21:47,160
‎Yes, Secretary Oh.

250
00:21:48,078 --> 00:21:49,704
‎I need you to look into someone for me.

251
00:21:50,622 --> 00:21:52,499
‎Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk from the Seoul
‎Central District Prosecutors' Office.

252
00:21:52,582 --> 00:21:53,500
‎Min-hwan.

253
00:22:01,341 --> 00:22:03,593
‎THE HOLY BIBLE

254
00:22:10,392 --> 00:22:13,145
‎-So you've finally settled on one?
‎-No.

255
00:22:13,728 --> 00:22:15,105
‎I went back to having no religion.

256
00:22:15,814 --> 00:22:16,815
‎What?

257
00:22:17,315 --> 00:22:18,400
‎I switched back.

258
00:22:19,151 --> 00:22:19,985
‎I see.

259
00:22:37,502 --> 00:22:38,712
‎I don't believe it.

260
00:22:44,301 --> 00:22:45,302
‎Jeez.

261
00:22:50,932 --> 00:22:52,058
‎Why did you want to see me?

262
00:22:53,894 --> 00:22:55,562
‎How much do you know about Yeo-ri?

263
00:22:58,732 --> 00:23:00,233
‎More than you think.

264
00:23:00,817 --> 00:23:01,902
‎I doubt that.

265
00:23:03,028 --> 00:23:04,571
‎You know she broke off her engagement

266
00:23:04,654 --> 00:23:06,573
‎with the son of Cha & Yul's
‎managing partner, right?

267
00:23:06,656 --> 00:23:08,783
‎I only heard about it
‎since I was abroad at the time.

268
00:23:08,867 --> 00:23:11,703
‎Then do you know why they broke it off?

269
00:23:13,663 --> 00:23:14,831
‎Do I have to know why?

270
00:23:15,832 --> 00:23:17,751
‎You told me before

271
00:23:18,460 --> 00:23:20,921
‎that if you care about someone,
‎you learn all about them.

272
00:23:21,004 --> 00:23:23,840
‎I thought you'd naturally want to know
‎why they broke it off.

273
00:23:26,635 --> 00:23:27,886
‎Don't you want to know?

274
00:23:27,969 --> 00:23:29,846
‎Some rumors started
‎after the engagement fell through.

275
00:23:29,930 --> 00:23:30,972
‎Ha-ri.

276
00:23:32,849 --> 00:23:34,935
‎If I want to know something,
‎I can look into it myself.

277
00:23:41,274 --> 00:23:43,818
‎Oh, that night at the hospital?

278
00:23:43,902 --> 00:23:45,028
‎I remember.

279
00:23:51,451 --> 00:23:52,744
‎You're where?

280
00:24:04,714 --> 00:24:07,300
‎An anonymous tip-off
‎leading to the discovery of a body.

281
00:24:08,009 --> 00:24:10,595
‎Doesn't it feel like ‎déjà vu?

282
00:24:11,096 --> 00:24:11,972
‎Yes.

283
00:24:27,195 --> 00:24:29,406
‎I don't need extra layers like these.

284
00:25:20,332 --> 00:25:22,125
‎You should go inside and warm up.

285
00:25:22,751 --> 00:25:24,711
‎Nice, we did it. High-five?

286
00:25:25,337 --> 00:25:26,671
‎Lend me a hand?

287
00:26:34,489 --> 00:26:36,574
‎-Enjoy your lunch.
‎-You too, sir.

288
00:26:43,915 --> 00:26:46,292
‎-Enjoy your lunch, sir!
‎-Thank you.

289
00:26:54,342 --> 00:26:56,219
‎Reina Hotel's slush fund allegations?

290
00:26:56,302 --> 00:26:58,054
‎Yeah. I sense some rising smoke.

291
00:26:58,138 --> 00:27:00,849
‎Rich people use art
‎to launder money, you know.

292
00:27:00,932 --> 00:27:03,017
‎-It's pretty large-scale too.
‎-Come on.

293
00:27:03,101 --> 00:27:05,854
‎It smoked a bit,
‎but the fire went out long ago.

294
00:27:15,363 --> 00:27:18,241
‎Ma'am, have you
‎not been sleeping well lately?

295
00:27:19,492 --> 00:27:20,869
‎Why do you ask?

296
00:27:20,952 --> 00:27:22,829
‎You look very tired.

297
00:27:32,380 --> 00:27:33,381
‎Who is that?

298
00:27:33,465 --> 00:27:36,634
‎That's Director Lee Hwa-yong
‎of the Yeeon Foundation.

299
00:27:37,927 --> 00:27:38,887
‎Yeeon Museum of Art.

300
00:27:39,512 --> 00:27:41,764
‎The director there is pretty influential.

301
00:27:43,641 --> 00:27:45,602
‎-Mr. Bong.
‎-Yes?

302
00:27:47,896 --> 00:27:49,856
‎Could you come a little closer?

303
00:27:49,939 --> 00:27:51,566
‎Pardon? Oh, sure.

304
00:27:55,695 --> 00:27:57,238
‎The artworks displayed at the hotel

305
00:27:57,322 --> 00:28:01,159
‎are brought in by the Art Team
‎through Director Ok,

306
00:28:01,242 --> 00:28:03,369
‎so Gallery Cheon supplies them, right?

307
00:28:03,453 --> 00:28:05,121
‎Yes, that is correct.

308
00:28:05,205 --> 00:28:08,374
‎Have we ever made
‎a direct purchase from Yeeon?

309
00:28:08,458 --> 00:28:11,127
‎No, not as far as I'm aware.

310
00:28:13,963 --> 00:28:16,382
‎Would you like me to look into it?

311
00:28:17,800 --> 00:28:20,970
‎No, I'll bring it up some other time.

312
00:28:22,347 --> 00:28:23,515
‎Don't stand too close.

313
00:28:24,265 --> 00:28:25,099
‎Oh, right.

314
00:28:28,394 --> 00:28:31,773
‎A 300-year-old love letter
‎written by Joseon-era

315
00:28:31,856 --> 00:28:35,735
‎courtesan-turned-poet Hwagyeongdang,
‎whose story was likened

316
00:28:35,818 --> 00:28:38,446
‎to the 1990 film ‎Ghost
‎recently came to light.

317
00:28:38,530 --> 00:28:40,782
‎It recently became the talk of the town.

318
00:28:40,865 --> 00:28:43,159
‎We asked Lee Hwa-yong,
‎the director of Yeeon Foundation,

319
00:28:43,243 --> 00:28:46,871
‎why she decided
‎to reveal the letter to the public.

320
00:28:46,955 --> 00:28:47,872
‎Well…

321
00:28:48,748 --> 00:28:52,585
‎We discovered this love letter
‎while relocating the tomb

322
00:28:52,669 --> 00:28:55,046
‎of my ancestor, Prince Gangpyeong.

323
00:28:55,129 --> 00:28:57,257
‎As many are already aware,

324
00:28:57,340 --> 00:29:00,552
‎the letter shows
‎Hwagyeongdang's ‎love ‎for Prince Gangpyeong

325
00:29:00,635 --> 00:29:03,304
‎that transcended class and social status.

326
00:29:04,138 --> 00:29:07,725
‎These days, there's so much violence
‎carried out in the name of love,

327
00:29:07,809 --> 00:29:10,854
‎so I wanted to remind us
‎what's most important

328
00:29:10,937 --> 00:29:13,606
‎and provide consolation
‎in what little way I can

329
00:29:13,690 --> 00:29:15,108
‎by displaying the letter.

330
00:29:16,526 --> 00:29:17,986
‎After the exhibition,

331
00:29:18,069 --> 00:29:21,614
‎I'll respect the wishes of my late father,
‎the foundation's first director,

332
00:29:21,698 --> 00:29:23,116
‎and donate it to his alma mater--

333
00:29:31,124 --> 00:29:32,333
‎Great shot.

334
00:29:33,751 --> 00:29:34,752
‎I'm playing decently today.

335
00:29:36,170 --> 00:29:37,088
‎It's really nice.

336
00:29:37,171 --> 00:29:40,008
‎A design that focuses
‎on harmonizing with nature.

337
00:29:40,091 --> 00:29:41,634
‎The layout is daring too.

338
00:29:41,718 --> 00:29:43,469
‎Is it Jackson Nicola's work?

339
00:29:43,553 --> 00:29:45,597
‎I paid a small fortune
‎to get the design right.

340
00:29:46,389 --> 00:29:47,348
‎Come and play often.

341
00:29:47,932 --> 00:29:49,851
‎Just gather a solid group first.

342
00:29:50,685 --> 00:29:51,561
‎Right.

343
00:29:52,061 --> 00:29:55,148
‎You went to school with Cha Gi-u
‎from Cha & Yul Law Firm, right?

344
00:29:55,231 --> 00:29:57,775
‎Yeah, he's one of our members.
‎Should I set up a round with him?

345
00:29:59,903 --> 00:30:01,029
‎Sure.

346
00:30:01,112 --> 00:30:02,030
‎Okay.

347
00:30:05,158 --> 00:30:06,451
‎-I need to take this.
‎-Sure.

348
00:30:07,994 --> 00:30:09,120
‎Hey, Yeo-ri.

349
00:30:12,874 --> 00:30:14,292
‎Sure, let's go together.

350
00:30:15,168 --> 00:30:16,711
‎I'll pick you up.

351
00:30:16,794 --> 00:30:18,338
‎-What is it?
‎-Just get in there.

352
00:30:18,421 --> 00:30:19,797
‎-Hurry up.
‎-What's this about?

353
00:30:20,673 --> 00:30:22,508
‎Come on and sit over there.

354
00:30:23,343 --> 00:30:25,053
‎And drink this. It's the latte you like.

355
00:30:26,262 --> 00:30:27,221
‎Sit.

356
00:30:28,139 --> 00:30:29,057
‎What's up?

357
00:30:30,016 --> 00:30:31,017
‎Hey.

358
00:30:31,100 --> 00:30:35,188
‎Tell me all you know
‎about what you said in the cafeteria.

359
00:30:35,813 --> 00:30:36,773
‎About what?

360
00:30:37,690 --> 00:30:38,942
‎The Reina Hotel slush fund.

361
00:30:39,525 --> 00:30:41,569
‎Oh, that?

362
00:30:42,320 --> 00:30:43,696
‎You want me to talk for free?

363
00:30:43,780 --> 00:30:45,531
‎I got you coffee.

364
00:30:47,951 --> 00:30:49,577
‎How about a meal?

365
00:30:49,661 --> 00:30:51,371
‎A meal? I'll buy you food too.

366
00:30:51,454 --> 00:30:52,789
‎Here. Drink this.

367
00:30:52,872 --> 00:30:54,707
‎Not the cafeteria. Somewhere else.

368
00:30:54,791 --> 00:30:56,584
‎Okay, fine.

369
00:30:57,126 --> 00:30:58,544
‎What's the smoke you saw?

370
00:30:58,628 --> 00:31:00,713
‎I'll pick the time and location then.

371
00:31:02,298 --> 00:31:04,258
‎Deal. Now start talking.

372
00:31:04,342 --> 00:31:05,426
‎This is perfect.

373
00:31:05,510 --> 00:31:07,011
‎-We'll make it if we go now.
‎-Where?

374
00:31:07,095 --> 00:31:09,722
‎You said I could decide
‎on the time and location.

375
00:31:09,806 --> 00:31:11,641
‎Not right now. I have to work late.

376
00:31:11,724 --> 00:31:12,892
‎Do that after eating with me.

377
00:31:12,976 --> 00:31:14,310
‎-Come along.
‎-But…

378
00:31:14,394 --> 00:31:16,813
‎-Hey, you really need to fix that.
‎-Hurry.

379
00:31:17,313 --> 00:31:18,272
‎Let me get my coat.

380
00:31:19,357 --> 00:31:20,817
‎This is where you wanted to eat?

381
00:31:20,900 --> 00:31:23,277
‎Yeah. I wanted to come
‎to a place like this with you.

382
00:31:23,361 --> 00:31:24,612
‎Hey, Gang-uk.

383
00:31:24,696 --> 00:31:27,281
‎What the heck was that about?

384
00:31:27,949 --> 00:31:29,784
‎This isn't my taste.
‎Let's go someplace else.

385
00:31:30,785 --> 00:31:33,955
‎Then I'll forget all I know
‎about Reina Hotel and its slush fund.

386
00:31:34,914 --> 00:31:36,165
‎What event are we here for?

387
00:31:37,166 --> 00:31:38,042
‎That one.

388
00:31:38,835 --> 00:31:41,421
‎You haven't heard of it?
‎It's been a hot topic lately.

389
00:31:41,504 --> 00:31:44,924
‎They're hosting a special unveiling today
‎before showing it to the public.

390
00:31:45,842 --> 00:31:47,552
‎How did you get invited
‎to something like this?

391
00:31:47,635 --> 00:31:52,223
‎I got to know the director here
‎while investigating an art theft case.

392
00:31:53,182 --> 00:31:55,393
‎You know, she set me up

393
00:31:55,476 --> 00:31:58,604
‎on a few blind dates with some great guys.

394
00:31:58,688 --> 00:32:01,482
‎You could've brought
‎one of them here instead.

395
00:32:01,566 --> 00:32:04,736
‎-Why drag poor busy me here?
‎-You're not getting it, are you?

396
00:32:05,236 --> 00:32:06,988
‎I wanted to bring you.

397
00:32:07,989 --> 00:32:10,575
‎Fine, whatever.
‎Where are they showing that letter?

398
00:32:10,658 --> 00:32:12,744
‎Probably somewhere indoors. Let's go.

399
00:32:14,287 --> 00:32:15,288
‎It's so pretty.

400
00:32:33,848 --> 00:32:39,437
‎WAITING FOR A LOVE LETTER AFTER 300 YEARS

401
00:32:40,063 --> 00:32:42,482
‎Hey, I look horrible. Delete it.

402
00:32:42,565 --> 00:32:44,233
‎No one told you to scowl.

403
00:32:45,651 --> 00:32:47,361
‎-Hey.
‎-Wow.

404
00:32:47,445 --> 00:32:49,864
‎So the 300-year-old love letter
‎is in that glass case?

405
00:32:49,947 --> 00:32:51,240
‎It looks like it.

406
00:32:52,075 --> 00:32:53,034
‎Prosecutor Im.

407
00:32:53,117 --> 00:32:54,494
‎-Hello, Director.
‎-Hi.

408
00:32:54,577 --> 00:32:56,037
‎Thank you for the invitation.

409
00:32:56,120 --> 00:32:58,873
‎-Thanks so much for coming.
‎-Of course.

410
00:32:58,956 --> 00:33:00,291
‎Who might this be?

411
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:03,211
‎He's a colleague of mine,
‎Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk.

412
00:33:03,294 --> 00:33:05,755
‎-I see. Nice to meet you.
‎-It's a pleasure.

413
00:33:05,838 --> 00:33:07,840
‎-Would you come and say hello?
‎-Sure.

414
00:33:40,331 --> 00:33:41,999
‎-Let's go, Ma.
‎-What?

415
00:33:43,626 --> 00:33:44,460
‎Let's go.

416
00:33:44,544 --> 00:33:45,378
‎Yeo-ri.

417
00:33:46,504 --> 00:33:47,338
‎Right.

418
00:33:47,421 --> 00:33:49,006
‎-Let's go.
‎-Let go of me.

419
00:33:58,641 --> 00:33:59,851
‎Yeo-ri.

420
00:34:02,019 --> 00:34:05,690
‎Thank you for making
‎the long journey over.

421
00:34:05,773 --> 00:34:09,443
‎I'm Lee Hwa-yong,
‎Director of the Yeeon Foundation.

422
00:34:13,531 --> 00:34:15,324
‎-What are you looking at?
‎-Look straight ahead.

423
00:34:15,408 --> 00:34:18,870
‎My late father built
‎the Yeeon Museum of Art

424
00:34:18,953 --> 00:34:21,622
‎where Prince Gangpyeong's
‎residence once stood…

425
00:34:21,706 --> 00:34:24,208
‎Why does he always stare at me like that?

426
00:34:24,292 --> 00:34:27,545
‎It makes me emotional
‎that I can unveil the letter here today.

427
00:34:27,628 --> 00:34:31,883
‎I will now unveil the love letter
‎of Hwagyeongdang,

428
00:34:31,966 --> 00:34:35,845
‎who was a great poet of her time
‎and also a respected painter.

429
00:34:58,868 --> 00:34:59,869
‎Is it breaking?

430
00:35:07,460 --> 00:35:09,587
‎-It's about to crack.
‎-Oh, no!

431
00:35:13,758 --> 00:35:15,009
‎Ms. Kim.

432
00:35:29,482 --> 00:35:30,691
‎Our apologies.

433
00:35:30,775 --> 00:35:33,319
‎This event is cancelled,
‎and we'll inform you of further plans.

434
00:35:33,402 --> 00:35:34,528
‎We're very sorry.

435
00:35:35,321 --> 00:35:36,447
‎Please stay calm.

436
00:35:36,530 --> 00:35:39,033
‎You can take the stairs and exit safely.

437
00:35:39,617 --> 00:35:41,911
‎We apologize for the disturbance.
‎Show them the way.

438
00:35:42,453 --> 00:35:43,746
‎What on earth was that?

439
00:35:43,829 --> 00:35:46,082
‎-Are you hurt?
‎-Moving a tomb can bring bad luck.

440
00:35:46,165 --> 00:35:47,708
‎-Watch your step.
‎-Is that what happened?

441
00:35:47,792 --> 00:35:49,293
‎It must be that.

442
00:35:49,377 --> 00:35:51,629
‎Why would a glass case break
‎when no one touched it?

443
00:35:51,712 --> 00:35:52,713
‎I know, right?

444
00:35:53,714 --> 00:35:55,383
‎This doesn't feel right.

445
00:35:55,466 --> 00:35:57,343
‎-It feels ominous.
‎-Let's get out of here.

446
00:35:57,426 --> 00:35:59,178
‎Leave slowly, one at a time.

447
00:36:00,221 --> 00:36:02,723
‎-What do you think happened?
‎-The glass shattered.

448
00:36:02,807 --> 00:36:05,685
‎-What a shoddy job.
‎-Make sure you have your belongings.

449
00:36:05,768 --> 00:36:08,562
‎-Why would a perfectly fine glass break?
‎-It felt so strange.

450
00:36:09,146 --> 00:36:10,231
‎Aren't you coming?

451
00:36:10,314 --> 00:36:11,482
‎I have to go somewhere.

452
00:36:11,565 --> 00:36:13,317
‎-I'll come with you.
‎-No, no.

453
00:36:14,694 --> 00:36:16,696
‎My stomach hurts.
‎I'm going to the bathroom.

454
00:36:16,779 --> 00:36:19,198
‎-You go ahead. Bye.
‎-What?

455
00:36:27,081 --> 00:36:28,958
‎I came here for a meeting
‎at my mother's request.

456
00:36:29,041 --> 00:36:30,710
‎Can I quickly go and say hello?

457
00:36:31,460 --> 00:36:32,837
‎Yeah, sure. Go ahead.

458
00:36:32,920 --> 00:36:35,381
‎-Sorry. Look around in the meantime.
‎-Okay.

459
00:36:58,988 --> 00:37:03,284
‎The legal team will file for damages
‎against the glass manufacturer.

460
00:37:03,367 --> 00:37:04,368
‎Our apologies, ma'am.

461
00:37:05,828 --> 00:37:06,787
‎What for?

462
00:37:06,871 --> 00:37:09,165
‎Will you make them pay
‎for the broken glass?

463
00:37:09,248 --> 00:37:11,959
‎Is this how you think
‎an unveiling should go?

464
00:37:12,043 --> 00:37:14,587
‎What will you do about the humiliation?

465
00:37:15,463 --> 00:37:16,297
‎What?

466
00:37:19,967 --> 00:37:20,843
‎Oh, Mr. Kang.

467
00:37:22,636 --> 00:37:24,555
‎-You must've been shocked earlier.
‎-Not at all.

468
00:37:25,639 --> 00:37:27,933
‎We'll arrange another unveiling
‎to make up for it.

469
00:37:28,434 --> 00:37:29,435
‎Okay.

470
00:37:52,958 --> 00:37:53,918
‎Hey, Yeo-ri.

471
00:37:54,543 --> 00:37:56,087
‎You're still here?

472
00:37:56,754 --> 00:37:57,922
‎Yes.

473
00:37:59,173 --> 00:38:03,177
‎I didn't get to properly say hi earlier
‎when we've met again after a while.

474
00:38:05,554 --> 00:38:06,639
‎How have you been?

475
00:38:07,681 --> 00:38:09,975
‎I've been doing fine, I guess.

476
00:38:11,018 --> 00:38:12,353
‎So we meet again.

477
00:38:13,521 --> 00:38:14,855
‎Are you doing well too?

478
00:38:14,939 --> 00:38:16,524
‎Yes, of course. I'm great.

479
00:38:19,110 --> 00:38:21,445
‎You seem to have solved
‎another case by the river.

480
00:38:21,529 --> 00:38:23,697
‎That's what I do as usual.

481
00:38:23,781 --> 00:38:24,740
‎Right.

482
00:38:29,036 --> 00:38:29,870
‎Bye then.

483
00:38:32,456 --> 00:38:34,875
‎Wait. Just a moment.

484
00:38:39,422 --> 00:38:41,048
‎I'm not doing well, actually.

485
00:38:44,677 --> 00:38:45,761
‎The thing is…

486
00:38:45,845 --> 00:38:48,931
‎Are you unwell because of the accident?

487
00:38:49,014 --> 00:38:50,266
‎No, it's not that.

488
00:38:53,477 --> 00:38:54,603
‎I still see them.

489
00:38:56,689 --> 00:38:57,773
‎I mean,

490
00:38:57,857 --> 00:39:00,109
‎I still see ghosts and I'm struggling.

491
00:39:00,860 --> 00:39:02,695
‎No way. That can't be.

492
00:39:02,778 --> 00:39:05,906
‎I still see ghosts all the time,

493
00:39:05,990 --> 00:39:07,908
‎and they give me a fright.

494
00:39:07,992 --> 00:39:11,537
‎I wasn't sure
‎if I should contact you about it,

495
00:39:11,620 --> 00:39:13,330
‎and we happened to meet here today.

496
00:39:16,083 --> 00:39:17,168
‎Then…

497
00:39:17,793 --> 00:39:21,338
‎do you see the ghost that's here with us?

498
00:39:21,422 --> 00:39:22,339
‎What?

499
00:39:23,924 --> 00:39:25,009
‎Yes, I see it.

500
00:39:25,092 --> 00:39:26,218
‎What does it look like?

501
00:39:29,763 --> 00:39:30,931
‎It's wearing ‎hanbok‎,

502
00:39:31,432 --> 00:39:32,600
‎the traditional Korean outfit.

503
00:39:35,686 --> 00:39:36,937
‎-What else?
‎-What else?

504
00:39:37,021 --> 00:39:38,564
‎Go on. What does it look like?

505
00:39:40,983 --> 00:39:43,694
‎It's wearing a jade ‎binyeo‎,
‎that fancy hairpin, and is very graceful.

506
00:39:44,361 --> 00:39:45,821
‎-What else?
‎-What else?

507
00:39:45,905 --> 00:39:49,074
‎Do you see a small black mole
‎under an eye?

508
00:39:49,158 --> 00:39:51,118
‎Yes, I do. There's a mole under one eye.

509
00:39:51,202 --> 00:39:53,871
‎-And is there a knife in her mouth?
‎-Yes. I feel her resentment.

510
00:39:53,954 --> 00:39:56,457
‎She's glaring at me
‎with the knife in her mouth…

511
00:39:58,751 --> 00:40:01,795
‎What prosecutor is this good at lying?

512
00:40:05,049 --> 00:40:06,509
‎You could tell?

513
00:40:07,468 --> 00:40:09,970
‎How did you know it was wearing ‎hanbok‎?

514
00:40:10,763 --> 00:40:11,805
‎Well, this place

515
00:40:11,889 --> 00:40:14,099
‎felt like the set of a period drama,

516
00:40:14,183 --> 00:40:17,186
‎and those portraits stood out
‎the moment you asked.

517
00:40:18,395 --> 00:40:21,023
‎And the jade ‎binyeo‎.
‎Where did that idea come from?

518
00:40:21,106 --> 00:40:24,443
‎People wearing ‎hanbok
‎tend to wear one or two of them.

519
00:40:25,486 --> 00:40:28,405
‎How did you catch on right away?

520
00:40:31,158 --> 00:40:32,660
‎Because it's not a woman.

521
00:40:33,744 --> 00:40:34,745
‎It's a man.

522
00:40:35,746 --> 00:40:36,747
‎What?

523
00:40:39,625 --> 00:40:41,627
‎Then is there really one…

524
00:40:44,129 --> 00:40:45,381
‎next to me?

525
00:40:47,132 --> 00:40:48,842
‎Yes, he's right next to you.

526
00:40:55,099 --> 00:40:56,934
‎I'm sorry, I'll be careful.

527
00:40:58,602 --> 00:41:01,647
‎Ms. Cheon,
‎is there something wrong with this place?

528
00:41:02,773 --> 00:41:04,942
‎Well, I can't say for sure just yet.

529
00:41:06,068 --> 00:41:08,028
‎I need to look into it some more.

530
00:41:08,112 --> 00:41:09,780
‎Right. I see.

531
00:41:13,158 --> 00:41:14,076
‎Ms. Cheon.

532
00:41:14,994 --> 00:41:16,537
‎Why don't we work together?

533
00:41:17,454 --> 00:41:18,289
‎On what?

534
00:41:18,372 --> 00:41:21,166
‎I don't know what exactly,

535
00:41:21,250 --> 00:41:23,252
‎but this feels huge and historical.

536
00:41:24,003 --> 00:41:27,464
‎It might be better to cooperate
‎than to work on your own.

537
00:41:28,215 --> 00:41:30,801
‎You can handle the dead,
‎and I can handle the living.

538
00:41:30,884 --> 00:41:33,304
‎This is my thing.
‎I'm on the Cold Case Unit.

539
00:41:33,387 --> 00:41:34,972
‎How about we work together--

540
00:41:35,055 --> 00:41:36,056
‎You're still here?

541
00:41:38,225 --> 00:41:39,059
‎Yes.

542
00:41:40,603 --> 00:41:42,396
‎Think about it. I'll wait for your call.

543
00:41:52,865 --> 00:41:53,866
‎Let's go.

544
00:41:55,242 --> 00:41:56,076
‎Okay.

545
00:42:19,391 --> 00:42:20,893
‎"You're still here?"

546
00:42:25,648 --> 00:42:26,982
‎I need a beer.

547
00:42:30,235 --> 00:42:31,362
‎Ms. Cheon.

548
00:42:31,445 --> 00:42:32,988
‎Why don't we work together?

549
00:42:33,072 --> 00:42:35,866
‎You can handle the dead,
‎and I can handle the living.

550
00:42:39,828 --> 00:42:41,872
‎-Let's go, Ma.
‎-What?

551
00:43:09,191 --> 00:43:10,275
‎Hey, Min-hwan.

552
00:43:12,027 --> 00:43:13,404
‎It's me.

553
00:43:18,575 --> 00:43:21,912
‎Director Ok,
‎should we acquire another masterpiece?

554
00:43:23,706 --> 00:43:24,707
‎Pardon?

555
00:43:24,790 --> 00:43:26,917
‎I like how our last purchase went.

556
00:43:27,000 --> 00:43:28,585
‎It was the easiest to clean up.

557
00:43:28,669 --> 00:43:30,504
‎Won't it be a bit too risky

558
00:43:31,213 --> 00:43:33,173
‎to employ the same tactic twice?

559
00:43:33,257 --> 00:43:35,759
‎You see, the thing is…

560
00:43:35,843 --> 00:43:36,802
‎CEO KANG MIN-HWAN

561
00:43:36,885 --> 00:43:38,637
‎Goodness, excuse me.

562
00:43:39,304 --> 00:43:40,723
‎Hey, Mr. Kang.

563
00:43:40,806 --> 00:43:42,683
‎Yes, what is it, Min-hwan?

564
00:43:44,309 --> 00:43:45,436
‎What?

565
00:43:46,395 --> 00:43:47,730
‎Cheon Yeo-ri did?

566
00:43:55,571 --> 00:43:56,655
‎Ms. Cheon.

567
00:43:57,281 --> 00:43:59,908
‎-Hello, I'm Cheon Yeo-ri.
‎-Goodness.

568
00:43:59,992 --> 00:44:02,077
‎I didn't get to introduce myself
‎properly yesterday.

569
00:44:02,161 --> 00:44:03,912
‎Oh, about that.

570
00:44:03,996 --> 00:44:06,874
‎You must've been so disappointed.

571
00:44:06,957 --> 00:44:09,543
‎-It was such a humiliation.
‎-Not at all.

572
00:44:09,626 --> 00:44:12,337
‎I've hosted enough events to know
‎that things happen,

573
00:44:12,421 --> 00:44:13,839
‎however well you're prepared.

574
00:44:15,549 --> 00:44:17,843
‎Thank you for being so understanding.

575
00:44:19,052 --> 00:44:20,596
‎I wondered why

576
00:44:20,679 --> 00:44:24,433
‎you'd take so much interest
‎in something like this.

577
00:44:24,516 --> 00:44:28,187
‎Min-hwan tells me you studied
‎Archaeology and Art History.

578
00:44:29,229 --> 00:44:32,816
‎I assumed you'd have studied
‎Hotel Management or something like that.

579
00:44:32,900 --> 00:44:34,777
‎Thank you for your time, Director.

580
00:44:34,860 --> 00:44:36,236
‎Don't mention it.

581
00:44:36,320 --> 00:44:38,363
‎You can ask me anything you want.

582
00:44:39,573 --> 00:44:42,075
‎May I ask who drew these portraits?

583
00:44:42,743 --> 00:44:43,827
‎Oh, yes.

584
00:44:44,912 --> 00:44:46,580
‎That would be Dowon.

585
00:44:46,663 --> 00:44:49,166
‎He wasn't acknowledged
‎or appreciated in his time.

586
00:44:51,585 --> 00:44:55,088
‎Could I take another look
‎at the love letter?

587
00:44:55,172 --> 00:44:56,381
‎Yes, of course.

588
00:44:56,965 --> 00:44:58,091
‎Come this way.

589
00:45:01,470 --> 00:45:04,473
‎If this was found while relocating
‎Prince Gangpyeong's tomb,

590
00:45:04,556 --> 00:45:07,601
‎then was this love letter found
‎inside his coffin?

591
00:45:08,101 --> 00:45:09,102
‎Yes.

592
00:45:10,604 --> 00:45:12,898
‎Don't you find that so romantic?

593
00:45:12,981 --> 00:45:15,734
‎He must've yearned for her so deeply

594
00:45:15,817 --> 00:45:18,695
‎to have taken this letter
‎with him to death.

595
00:45:29,706 --> 00:45:32,668
‎It would have been a scandal in their day.

596
00:45:33,168 --> 00:45:36,338
‎Prince Gangpyeong was a royal
‎who loved a woman beneath his class,

597
00:45:36,421 --> 00:45:40,092
‎a ‎gisaeng,‎ a courtesan,
‎enough to make her his second wife.

598
00:45:44,930 --> 00:45:48,308
‎Where was Hwagyeongdang buried then?

599
00:45:48,392 --> 00:45:50,686
‎According to the story
‎told over generations,

600
00:45:50,769 --> 00:45:54,481
‎Prince Gangpyeong took her
‎on an excursion to Mt. Geumgang,

601
00:45:54,565 --> 00:45:57,401
‎where Hwagyeongdang vanished
‎without‎ a ‎trace.

602
00:45:58,610 --> 00:46:02,155
‎One version of the story says
‎she became an immortal hermit.

603
00:46:03,991 --> 00:46:06,827
‎I suppose that's how legends are made.

604
00:46:13,625 --> 00:46:15,294
‎Isn't it beautiful?

605
00:46:17,129 --> 00:46:21,633
‎Even down in the south,
‎such bright red camellias are rare.

606
00:46:22,301 --> 00:46:26,888
‎This isn't the time of year
‎for them to be in full bloom like that.

607
00:46:26,972 --> 00:46:29,850
‎So for the flowers to bloom
‎all of a sudden

608
00:46:29,933 --> 00:46:33,020
‎can only be a sign
‎of good things to come.

609
00:46:34,229 --> 00:46:36,231
‎What do you mean by that?

610
00:46:36,315 --> 00:46:40,611
‎The camellias must've known
‎that the love letter would be found.

611
00:46:41,194 --> 00:46:42,529
‎Just look at that sight.

612
00:46:52,039 --> 00:46:53,915
‎Here. Now get to it.

613
00:46:53,999 --> 00:46:56,501
‎-It's just a rumor, okay?
‎-Okay.

614
00:46:57,336 --> 00:46:59,296
‎A prosecutor went abroad
‎on a business trip

615
00:46:59,379 --> 00:47:01,298
‎and bought a pretty expensive painting.

616
00:47:01,381 --> 00:47:02,841
‎Since when do prosecutors do that?

617
00:47:02,924 --> 00:47:04,968
‎It's verified that they bought a painting,

618
00:47:05,052 --> 00:47:06,678
‎but there's no record of it
‎clearing customs.

619
00:47:08,096 --> 00:47:11,475
‎If customs has no record of it,
‎then either it didn't enter the country

620
00:47:11,558 --> 00:47:14,519
‎or someone powerful enough
‎to override customs was involved.

621
00:47:15,979 --> 00:47:17,689
‎A diplomatic pouch or Air Force One?

622
00:47:18,857 --> 00:47:21,860
‎That must've let off serious smoke.
‎Why didn't they dig further?

623
00:47:22,444 --> 00:47:23,695
‎It's not that they didn't. They couldn't.

624
00:47:24,905 --> 00:47:26,490
‎The person who bought the painting

625
00:47:28,408 --> 00:47:29,868
‎was Chief Prosecutor Ok Gye-dong.

626
00:47:30,827 --> 00:47:34,790
‎His older sister is Director Ok Gye-hui
‎of Reina Hotels & Resorts.

627
00:47:35,290 --> 00:47:36,583
‎Do you see where this is going?

628
00:47:38,168 --> 00:47:42,714
‎Does that mean Director Ok is involved
‎in Reina's money-laundering scheme?

629
00:47:43,507 --> 00:47:46,426
‎Whether it's money laundering or bribery,

630
00:47:46,510 --> 00:47:49,137
‎someone inside Reina
‎could be up to something.

631
00:47:52,140 --> 00:47:54,601
‎No way. I knew it.

632
00:47:54,685 --> 00:47:55,644
‎Knew what?

633
00:47:55,727 --> 00:47:57,896
‎Look. They're birds of a feather.

634
00:47:57,979 --> 00:47:59,564
‎REINA'S CHEON YEO-RI
‎DATING CL SUCCESSOR KANG MIN-HWAN

635
00:47:59,648 --> 00:48:01,858
‎THE PAIR ATTENDED
‎AN OFFICIAL EVENT TOGETHER…

636
00:48:03,402 --> 00:48:04,236
‎What the…

637
00:48:05,153 --> 00:48:07,447
‎They were dating?

638
00:48:12,369 --> 00:48:13,870
‎REINA'S CHEON YEO-RI
‎DATING CL SUCCESSOR KANG MIN-HWAN

639
00:48:18,250 --> 00:48:20,919
‎You seem to have solved
‎another case by the river.

640
00:48:21,002 --> 00:48:22,796
‎That's what I do as usual.

641
00:48:24,631 --> 00:48:26,883
‎-Investigator Ko?
‎-Yes?

642
00:48:26,967 --> 00:48:28,802
‎Have we been getting any tip-offs?

643
00:48:30,053 --> 00:48:33,432
‎You know, like we did for Mt. Haewang
‎or the river body case.

644
00:48:33,515 --> 00:48:35,976
‎No, we haven't gotten any recently.

645
00:48:36,059 --> 00:48:39,229
‎Well, have you been slacking lately?

646
00:48:39,813 --> 00:48:41,648
‎Or maybe things have
‎fallen through the cracks.

647
00:48:41,732 --> 00:48:44,860
‎If you say that,
‎that would be my sign to burst into tears.

648
00:48:44,943 --> 00:48:46,653
‎I'd be so hurt and upset.

649
00:48:46,737 --> 00:48:52,075
‎I don't know what riled you up so badly
‎that you're taking it out on me…

650
00:48:52,159 --> 00:48:53,785
‎-I'm not riled up.
‎-Okay.

651
00:48:53,869 --> 00:48:57,664
‎We're supposed to solve cold cases,
‎but it's way too quiet.

652
00:48:57,748 --> 00:49:00,459
‎Did you leave your post for hours
‎when you were on night duty?

653
00:49:00,542 --> 00:49:02,461
‎-You too.
‎-What? No.

654
00:49:02,544 --> 00:49:03,795
‎-Come on, man.
‎-What?

655
00:49:03,879 --> 00:49:05,547
‎No, sorry. I mean, Mr. Ma.

656
00:49:05,630 --> 00:49:07,466
‎Right. Mr. Ma.

657
00:49:07,549 --> 00:49:09,926
‎If that's how you feel, from now on,

658
00:49:10,010 --> 00:49:13,096
‎whenever I get a work call
‎or need to use the bathroom,

659
00:49:13,180 --> 00:49:15,432
‎I'll call you to report
‎every single detail.

660
00:49:15,515 --> 00:49:17,142
‎So that you're satisfied.

661
00:49:17,893 --> 00:49:18,727
‎That's it.

662
00:49:18,810 --> 00:49:22,481
‎That's why I must be involved,
‎even when it's you on night duty.

663
00:49:23,148 --> 00:49:25,776
‎Be sure to call me
‎especially if you get any tip-offs.

664
00:49:25,859 --> 00:49:26,943
‎Okay? You too, Hyeong-min.

665
00:49:27,027 --> 00:49:28,779
‎-Yes, of course.
‎-Okay.

666
00:49:29,821 --> 00:49:30,864
‎We'll work really hard.

667
00:49:36,953 --> 00:49:38,163
‎I can see you.

668
00:49:51,593 --> 00:49:53,970
‎Min-hwan said it wasn't him. Was it you?

669
00:49:54,054 --> 00:49:55,180
‎Take a seat.

670
00:49:59,017 --> 00:50:01,728
‎It's not a marriage announcement,
‎so what's the big deal?

671
00:50:01,812 --> 00:50:04,231
‎-It's up by how many percent?
‎-Thirteen percent, ma'am.

672
00:50:04,815 --> 00:50:05,982
‎My goodness.

673
00:50:06,066 --> 00:50:08,985
‎That's how the market reacted
‎to Reina and CL.

674
00:50:09,069 --> 00:50:11,154
‎You said you'd give me time.

675
00:50:11,238 --> 00:50:12,405
‎And I will.

676
00:50:12,489 --> 00:50:14,825
‎But I also need you
‎to give Min-hwan some hope.

677
00:50:16,409 --> 00:50:17,244
‎Grandma.

678
00:50:21,164 --> 00:50:23,583
‎-You can't barge in like that.
‎-I know what I'm doing.

679
00:50:31,049 --> 00:50:34,386
‎I heard the news about you and Min-hwan
‎was the chairwoman's idea.

680
00:50:34,469 --> 00:50:35,929
‎Did you ask her for a favor?

681
00:50:37,764 --> 00:50:40,642
‎I must ask, only out of pure curiosity.

682
00:50:41,768 --> 00:50:44,813
‎Are you doing this because
‎you really want to marry Min-hwan?

683
00:50:44,896 --> 00:50:45,814
‎Why do you care?

684
00:50:45,897 --> 00:50:47,148
‎This is insane.

685
00:50:47,941 --> 00:50:48,775
‎It's nonsensical.

686
00:50:48,859 --> 00:50:50,902
‎Why is it nonsensical?

687
00:50:50,986 --> 00:50:53,780
‎So you ‎are‎ interested in marrying him.

688
00:50:54,823 --> 00:50:57,158
‎Min-hwan and Ji-hwan were brothers.

689
00:50:57,784 --> 00:51:00,328
‎If I were you, seeing Min-hwan
‎would remind me of Ji-hwan--

690
00:51:00,412 --> 00:51:01,246
‎Cheon Ha-ri.

691
00:51:04,124 --> 00:51:04,958
‎What?

692
00:51:05,041 --> 00:51:06,459
‎That's enough. Get out.

693
00:51:29,566 --> 00:51:31,026
‎NANGMAN SALTED BEEF TRIPE

694
00:51:31,109 --> 00:51:33,528
‎No, you can't.

695
00:51:33,612 --> 00:51:35,030
‎Go away. Leave.

696
00:51:39,576 --> 00:51:42,329
‎Nice, pork skin.
‎Weren't they good last time?

697
00:51:45,624 --> 00:51:47,751
‎That's one place,
‎and that's the other place.

698
00:51:47,834 --> 00:51:49,502
‎We're spoiled with options.

699
00:51:49,586 --> 00:51:51,171
‎You don't know
‎how addictive pork skin is.

700
00:51:51,254 --> 00:51:53,381
‎Gang-uk, are you going for dinner?

701
00:51:55,091 --> 00:51:56,676
‎-Hello.
‎-You're walking arm-in-arm?

702
00:51:56,760 --> 00:51:59,554
‎-Are you eating out?
‎-Ms. Im, do you like pork skin?

703
00:51:59,638 --> 00:52:02,265
‎-I love pork skin.
‎-Great, then we can…

704
00:52:02,349 --> 00:52:04,476
‎How about we go over there?
‎Their pork skin is amazing.

705
00:52:04,559 --> 00:52:06,937
‎-You should join us.
‎-Sounds good.

706
00:52:07,020 --> 00:52:09,147
‎You can go and enjoy yourselves.

707
00:52:09,230 --> 00:52:10,774
‎-We reserved a table…
‎-Come on in.

708
00:52:10,857 --> 00:52:12,692
‎-Let's all eat together.
‎-I have to go.

709
00:52:12,776 --> 00:52:14,152
‎Why leave when you came all this way?

710
00:52:14,235 --> 00:52:15,487
‎I need to work late today.

711
00:52:15,570 --> 00:52:17,364
‎You work late more often than you eat.

712
00:52:17,447 --> 00:52:21,034
‎-Eat with us before you go.
‎-I'll just buy something on the way back.

713
00:52:21,117 --> 00:52:23,703
‎Enjoy your meal
‎with Pil-dong and Hyeong-min.

714
00:52:25,622 --> 00:52:27,874
‎-You're actually leaving?
‎-Enjoy yourself!

715
00:52:31,044 --> 00:52:31,962
‎All right, attention!

716
00:52:32,921 --> 00:52:36,049
‎Everyone who's waited for their turn,
‎show yourselves now.

717
00:52:44,766 --> 00:52:47,894
‎Today, it's not first-come, first-served.
‎I'll pick based on your predicament.

718
00:52:48,853 --> 00:52:51,982
‎"The vile one who got me
‎deserves nothing but a beating."

719
00:52:52,065 --> 00:52:55,485
‎"I want to make sure
‎they pay the price and rot in prison."

720
00:52:55,568 --> 00:52:56,403
‎Who has that kind of story?

721
00:52:58,279 --> 00:52:59,614
‎Talk to me.

722
00:53:02,200 --> 00:53:03,660
‎You first.

723
00:53:04,744 --> 00:53:06,997
‎3 DAYS AGO

724
00:53:07,080 --> 00:53:08,999
‎It was somewhere here.

725
00:53:09,082 --> 00:53:11,042
‎Can we just call it a day and go home?

726
00:53:11,960 --> 00:53:15,505
‎It looks like it'll rain soon,
‎and I have a bad feeling.

727
00:53:15,588 --> 00:53:18,550
‎It's fine. I saw a really pretty one here.

728
00:53:19,134 --> 00:53:21,261
‎-It's somewhere here.
‎-You did?

729
00:53:22,345 --> 00:53:24,222
‎-You're sure it's nearby?
‎-This is it.

730
00:53:24,723 --> 00:53:25,724
‎-Look.
‎-Really?

731
00:53:26,808 --> 00:53:27,767
‎Wow.

732
00:53:28,852 --> 00:53:30,186
‎You really found it.

733
00:53:31,855 --> 00:53:33,440
‎It's beautiful.

734
00:53:33,523 --> 00:53:35,483
‎Come and have a look.

735
00:54:02,719 --> 00:54:03,720
‎Hello?

736
00:54:19,652 --> 00:54:21,863
‎I should've stamped your fingerprint
‎before letting you go.

737
00:54:24,741 --> 00:54:26,284
‎I forgot about that, honey.

738
00:54:32,874 --> 00:54:34,918
‎WRITTEN WILL

739
00:54:43,593 --> 00:54:44,469
‎Who's there?

740
00:54:44,552 --> 00:54:46,721
‎Talk about killing someone twice.

741
00:54:47,430 --> 00:54:49,599
‎How could one come back to do that?

742
00:54:54,187 --> 00:54:55,980
‎A bastard like him
‎doesn't deserve to be human.

743
00:55:02,570 --> 00:55:04,614
‎Are you on your own? This late at night?

744
00:55:04,697 --> 00:55:07,492
‎Would I have come here with a lover,
‎this late at night?

745
00:55:07,575 --> 00:55:09,619
‎If you're a passerby, just pass on by.

746
00:55:10,453 --> 00:55:11,788
‎Why see something you shouldn't?

747
00:55:12,664 --> 00:55:14,541
‎I wish I could unsee that too.

748
00:55:14,624 --> 00:55:17,085
‎Oh, is that so?

749
00:55:21,714 --> 00:55:22,882
‎Damn it.

750
00:55:30,140 --> 00:55:31,432
‎You're not a bad fighter.

751
00:55:50,368 --> 00:55:52,620
‎Who are you? Who the hell are you?

752
00:55:52,704 --> 00:55:54,664
‎-Let go.
‎-Damn it.

753
00:56:02,630 --> 00:56:05,967
‎I'll make you regret this.

754
00:56:07,343 --> 00:56:08,678
‎What should I go for?

755
00:56:10,096 --> 00:56:11,097
‎Your face?

756
00:56:14,934 --> 00:56:15,768
‎You punk!

757
00:56:26,446 --> 00:56:27,822
‎Get out of the way, Yeo-ri!

758
00:56:58,937 --> 00:57:00,313
‎-Mr. Ma.
‎-Wait.

759
00:57:00,396 --> 00:57:02,273
‎I'm fine. I'm fine, really.

760
00:57:03,149 --> 00:57:04,317
‎Are you two an item?

761
00:57:05,360 --> 00:57:06,486
‎You have a knife?

762
00:57:10,865 --> 00:57:12,116
‎Damn it.

763
00:57:19,624 --> 00:57:20,708
‎-That hurts.
‎-Keep still.

764
00:57:22,168 --> 00:57:24,379
‎-Damn you.
‎-Are you okay, Yeo-ri?

765
00:57:26,089 --> 00:57:27,006
‎Okay.

766
00:58:02,584 --> 00:58:04,836
‎Let go of me, damn it!

767
00:58:06,170 --> 00:58:08,339
‎I saw your face, you punk.

768
00:58:08,423 --> 00:58:09,799
‎Sure, whatever.

769
00:58:25,106 --> 00:58:28,109
‎Seeing ghosts
‎isn't some kind of superpower.

770
00:58:28,192 --> 00:58:32,030
‎How can you be so fearless,
‎coming alone to a mountain this late?

771
00:58:32,655 --> 00:58:35,658
‎That's why I called in a report
‎before coming here.

772
00:58:35,742 --> 00:58:37,827
‎I cover all my bases
‎before I set in motion.

773
00:58:37,910 --> 00:58:40,038
‎Right. Then what was that just now?

774
00:58:40,121 --> 00:58:42,665
‎You could've been badly hurt
‎if not for me.

775
00:58:45,126 --> 00:58:48,463
‎Aren't you the one
‎who could've been badly hurt?

776
00:58:49,047 --> 00:58:51,633
‎How could you not even
‎land a kick properly?

777
00:58:52,467 --> 00:58:53,926
‎That was a mistake.

778
00:58:54,010 --> 00:58:57,221
‎I trained in taekwondo,
‎judo, hapkido, and boxing.

779
00:58:57,305 --> 00:58:58,890
‎You don't know how fit I am.

780
00:58:58,973 --> 00:59:00,933
‎Oh, you're so fit and well-trained

781
00:59:01,017 --> 00:59:03,561
‎that you can't land a kick
‎when it actually counts?

782
00:59:03,645 --> 00:59:04,562
‎I thought

783
00:59:05,146 --> 00:59:08,191
‎you'd thrown out your back
‎because of the way you landed.

784
00:59:08,274 --> 00:59:10,652
‎You're so cruel.

785
00:59:10,735 --> 00:59:14,322
‎I was on standby for days on end,
‎working late in case you called.

786
00:59:14,405 --> 00:59:15,490
‎You're not the police.

787
00:59:15,573 --> 00:59:18,368
‎What prosecutor works late
‎to wait for a tip-off?

788
00:59:18,451 --> 00:59:19,744
‎Are all prosecutors like that?

789
00:59:19,827 --> 00:59:22,163
‎No other prosecutor does this.

790
00:59:22,246 --> 00:59:23,915
‎I do it only because of you…

791
00:59:26,709 --> 00:59:27,543
‎What I mean is…

792
00:59:28,670 --> 00:59:34,133
‎I mean, I'm in charge of cold cases,
‎and we both used to see ghosts.

793
00:59:34,217 --> 00:59:35,802
‎I can't just turn a blind eye.

794
00:59:36,469 --> 00:59:37,970
‎Only my life is back to normal,

795
00:59:38,054 --> 00:59:41,766
‎while you stay up at night
‎because of ghosts.

796
00:59:43,184 --> 00:59:44,018
‎Right?

797
00:59:50,316 --> 00:59:52,276
‎So from what I gather,

798
00:59:53,319 --> 00:59:55,405
‎it looks like you're getting engaged
‎to your boyfriend.

799
00:59:56,322 --> 00:59:58,991
‎It said we were dating,
‎not that we were engaged.

800
01:00:00,201 --> 01:00:02,704
‎So it's true that you're dating him?

801
01:00:03,204 --> 01:00:05,081
‎That false report will be corrected soon.

802
01:00:05,164 --> 01:00:06,666
‎What? "False report"?

803
01:00:08,042 --> 01:00:09,335
‎It's a false report?

804
01:00:11,212 --> 01:00:12,088
‎Yes, and besides…

805
01:00:13,715 --> 01:00:15,550
‎Why do you care if I'm dating or not?

806
01:00:16,467 --> 01:00:22,306
‎You showed up to a special event
‎with your girlfriend proudly on your arm.

807
01:00:22,390 --> 01:00:23,224
‎"Special event"?

808
01:00:25,143 --> 01:00:26,394
‎You mean the art gallery?

809
01:00:26,477 --> 01:00:29,564
‎I didn't link arms with her.
‎She clung to me like that.

810
01:00:29,647 --> 01:00:31,315
‎She is not my girlfriend.

811
01:00:31,399 --> 01:00:33,860
‎She and I are like…

812
01:00:33,943 --> 01:00:36,112
‎We could never get close.

813
01:00:37,572 --> 01:00:40,158
‎We're like the Earth and the moon.

814
01:00:40,241 --> 01:00:42,076
‎That's how far apart we are.

815
01:00:43,244 --> 01:00:46,080
‎-Like the Earth and the moon?
‎-Yes.

816
01:00:46,164 --> 01:00:49,500
‎How lovely.
‎Those two always come as a pair.

817
01:00:51,002 --> 01:00:55,673
‎Are you upset
‎that Im and I showed up as a pair?

818
01:00:55,757 --> 01:00:57,508
‎I'm just stating a fact.

819
01:00:58,259 --> 01:01:00,219
‎Did I say I was upset?

820
01:01:03,765 --> 01:01:07,059
‎Well then, instead of
‎the Earth and the moon,

821
01:01:07,143 --> 01:01:10,313
‎how about we call it Neptune?

822
01:01:10,396 --> 01:01:12,190
‎Would you feel any less upset?

823
01:01:12,273 --> 01:01:14,150
‎I never said I was upset.

824
01:01:14,233 --> 01:01:15,359
‎Not that then.

825
01:01:15,443 --> 01:01:17,820
‎Then how about Andromeda?

826
01:01:17,904 --> 01:01:19,489
‎Andromeda sounds much better.

827
01:01:20,656 --> 01:01:21,491
‎Doesn't it?

828
01:01:22,074 --> 01:01:23,910
‎Is there anything farther away than that?

829
01:01:24,494 --> 01:01:25,536
‎A black hole?

830
01:01:27,330 --> 01:01:29,332
‎Not even a goodbye? Can't you at least…

831
01:01:30,500 --> 01:01:32,335
‎Can't she at least say goodbye?

832
01:01:33,336 --> 01:01:34,378
‎She didn't even bother.

833
01:02:21,300 --> 01:02:23,719
‎You said you handled cold cases.

834
01:02:24,220 --> 01:02:25,054
‎Yes.

835
01:02:26,138 --> 01:02:27,098
‎Shall we take it on?

836
01:02:28,766 --> 01:02:30,726
‎A 300-year-old cold case.

837
01:02:31,853 --> 01:02:32,770
‎Let's work together.

838
01:03:03,676 --> 01:03:05,595
‎FIND ME

839
01:03:24,030 --> 01:03:26,449
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

840
01:03:26,532 --> 01:03:29,827
‎It's not the Joseon-era version of ‎Ghost,
‎but a total psychopath.

841
01:03:29,911 --> 01:03:32,330
‎We'll do whatever it takes to find a way.

842
01:03:32,413 --> 01:03:34,206
‎There's no such thing as a perfect crime.

843
01:03:34,290 --> 01:03:36,542
‎What must be revealed will come to light.

844
01:03:36,626 --> 01:03:39,420
‎I need you to check that.
‎That's the part that involves the living.

845
01:03:39,503 --> 01:03:42,798
‎This looks more like
‎Ms. Cheon's part than mine.

846
01:03:42,882 --> 01:03:46,302
‎Do you think Yeo-ri is actually onto us?

847
01:03:46,385 --> 01:03:48,095
‎Yes, hello, Ms. Cheon.

848
01:03:48,596 --> 01:03:51,307
‎Are these all the artworks
‎displayed around the hotel?

849
01:03:51,390 --> 01:03:53,017
‎Why do you want to know that so badly?

850
01:03:54,310 --> 01:03:55,645
‎What is this?

851
01:03:55,728 --> 01:03:58,272
‎I got them on my business trip to Europe.
‎I thought they'd suit you.

852
01:03:58,356 --> 01:04:00,816
‎I read the article about you two.
‎Congratulations.

853
01:04:00,900 --> 01:04:03,277
‎Are Cheon Yeo-ri and Min-hwan
‎actually dating?

854
01:04:03,361 --> 01:04:06,864
‎Min-hwan will be able to support you
‎more than enough.

855
01:04:06,948 --> 01:04:09,575
‎Why are you so hard to reach?
‎You said you'd call me back.

856
01:04:09,659 --> 01:04:12,870
‎I might have to get engaged.

857
01:04:13,454 --> 01:04:14,497
‎What?

858
01:04:14,580 --> 01:04:19,293
‎Subtitle translation by: Jennifer Jean Lim

